# I will read or I will finish in Russian: прочита́ю
subtitle: "Say what you'll finish in Russian: за́втра я прочита́ю кни́гу, with the done verb's present endings, against бу́ду чита́ть весь ве́чер for the time it fills."
tags: ["russian","russian aspect","russian future tense","perfective verbs","прочитаю","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/aspect","grammar/future-tense"]
thumb: "band \"Reading or finished? Russian makes you say\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Commands in Russian: прочита́й!","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/66-russian-imperative-aspect.cast"}

